Lobium — native Web Audio farbling (seeded, per-profile). Deep surface #3 (after WebGL + canvas).

Perturbs the float audio-sample READBACK surfaces by an imperceptible, per-sample relative amount
(seeds.audio, uint32) so a rendered-audio fingerprint becomes stable-per-profile, distinct-per-seed, and
differs from the host — the analogue of the canvas/WebGL work for the audio surface. The perturbation is
the shared skia-free kernel lobium::FarbleAudioSamples (//components/lobium_fp/lobium_audio_farble.cc,
staged with the module — NOT part of this hook patch): data[k] *= (1 + eps), eps in [-1.5e-3, +1.5e-3]
(~ -56 dBFS, inaudible) a pure splitmix64 function of (seed, absolute sample index). Relative multiply is
scale-invariant/sign-preserving; per-sample (not a constant fudge factor) so dividing two seeded
fingerprints cannot recover one ratio. No BUILD.gn change (kernel lives in the already-wired lobium_fp
source_set); no config change (seeds.audio already parsed). This is a genuine native-only surface — a JS
override of getChannelData / analyser reads is itself a detectable tell, so CDP cannot do it cleanly.

Three hook points (all reading LobiumFpConfig::Current(), all guarded on seeds.audio != 0), chosen to
cover the readback surfaces WITHOUT touching playback or internal DSP state:

  1. OfflineAudioContext::FireCompletionEvent (offline_audio_context.cc) — THE dominant audio fingerprint
     vector (OfflineAudioContext + DynamicsCompressor -> getChannelData/copyFromChannel sum/hash, used by
     FingerprintJS / CreepJS). The offline render is COMPLETE and this main-thread event fires exactly
     once per context (the render thread already posted NotifyComplete), so we perturb the finished RESULT
     backing store IN PLACE, once, before it is exposed. getChannelData(), copyFromChannel(), and
     event.renderedBuffer all read this same store, so every readback path agrees by construction — no
     per-call compounding, object identity preserved. The SAME (seed, index) key is used for every channel
     (NOT a per-channel fold): honest Chrome upmixes mono to bit-identical channels, and a per-channel key
     would make them diverge — a trivial `channelData(0)[k] === channelData(1)[k]` oracle; one eps
     sequence keeps identical channels identical (the factor cancels in the inter-channel ratio) yet
     farbles genuinely-distinct channels distinctly. We never touch the realtime graph or any playback
     source — the offline result is a readback artifact.
  2. RealtimeAnalyser::GetFloatFrequencyData (realtime_analyser.cc) — perturbs ONLY the JS-visible
     destination span [0,len) AFTER the fill loop; the internal magnitude_buffer_ (FFT + smoothing source)
     is untouched, so smoothingTimeConstant continuity and real visualizers are unaffected.
  3. RealtimeAnalyser::GetFloatTimeDomainData (realtime_analyser.cc) — same, over input_buffer_'s JS copy.

Deliberately NOT hooked (audio_buffer.cc is untouched): getChannelData/copyFromChannel on a user-created
AudioBuffer (decoded app audio / a playback source) — proven bit-exact under a seed (maxdiff 0), so real
audio is never corrupted. See hooks.md for the documented KNOWN LIMITATIONS (AudioWorklet /
ScriptProcessorNode upstream taps, known-input ratio inversion, byte analyser paths) and their rationale.

Proven on Chromium 152.0.7928.0 (SwiftShader, headless):
  - Offline: getChannelData == copyFromChannel == re-read, baseline 41c67cf0 -> seedA 235885ed (stable) ->
    seedB 7b006b3c (distinct); slicesum shifts ~0.003% (imperceptible).
  - Analyser (sampled deterministically via OfflineAudioContext.suspend): freq/time farbled, stable per
    seed, distinct per seed, livebins 1024/1024.
  - Stereo oracle: mono upmixed to OfflineAudioContext(2,..) yields channelData(0) === channelData(1)
    (interChannelMaxDiff 0) even farbled — matches honest upmix.
  - Playback safety: a user createBuffer()+copyToChannel()+getChannelData/copyFromChannel is bit-exact
    (maxdiff 0) with a seed set.

Two hook points touch existing files (this patch); the kernel + BUILD.gn wiring are added files:
  1. third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/offline_audio_context.cc — offline result farble (Hook A).
  2. third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webaudio/realtime_analyser.cc — analyser float paths (Hooks B, C).
